{
  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "steer-stats-export-parity-test",
    "parent": "steer-preference-denominator-counter",
    "kind": "enabling",
    "title": "Make steerAuthority serialization struct-derived and add an export-parity test on the emitted JSON",
    "description": "Kill the field-drop class rather than patching another field. In spur-core/src/simulator/util_stats.rs, ensure the steerAuthority struct derives Serialize (no hand-written key list / no manual serialize_struct), and in spur-core/src/simulator/explorer.rs remove any explicit per-field copy of steerAuthority into the emitted stats object, forwarding the struct wholesale. Then add spur-core/tests/stats_export_parity.rs which runs a tiny in-process campaign (a few hundred runs, any config), serializes the produced util_stats to JSON, and asserts the steerAuthority object's key set is exactly equal to the struct's field set — failing with the missing/extra names printed. Include the currently-missing preferenceConsulted and preferenceSourceAbsent so the test fails on today's tree and passes after the forwarding fix. Re-run general_vr.json and record the observed values of preferenceConsulted / preferenceSourceAbsent. No policy change, no new config field.",
    "category": "tooling",
    "buildsOn": [
      "util_stats",
      "explorer serialization",
      "steer-authority-counter-rewire",
      "steer-preference-denominator-counter"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 4,
    "expectedCost": 1,
    "rationale": "Three steer experiments in a row have produced uninterpretable all-zero/absent readings because the export path is a hand-maintained key list that silently drops new fields, and the wiring tests assert in-process rather than on the artifact. Struct-derived serialization plus a key-set parity test makes every future counter hypothesis readable by construction instead of one-field-at-a-time.",
    "generalityArgument": "Purely a serialization/test-harness change over the stats struct; asserts key-set equality and references no handler, message type, protocol role, or invariant.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-29T23:45:00Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "[unparked iteration 5340] Down-scored from 6 because the new counters do reach the utilization export, but the structural fix (derive Serialize, delete the hand-maintained key list) still kills the class that ate three iterations; falsified if the serializer is already derive-based."
  },
